#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:1
msgid "llvm-bcanalyzer - LLVM bitcode analyzer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-bcanalyzer` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-bcanalyzer` command is a small utility for analyzing "
"bitcode files. The tool reads a bitcode file (such as generated with the "
"{program}`llvm-as` tool) and produces a statistical report on the contents "
"of the bitcode file. The tool can also dump a low level but human-readable "
"version of the bitcode file. This tool is probably not of much interest or "
"utility except for those working directly with the bitcode file format. Most "
"LLVM users can just ignore this tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:20
msgid ""
"If *filename* is omitted or is `-`, then {program}`llvm-bcanalyzer` reads "
"its input from standard input. This is useful for combining the tool into a "
"pipeline. Output is written to the standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:24
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:30
msgid ""
"Causes {program}`llvm-bcanalyzer` to dump the bitcode in a human-readable "
"format. This format is significantly different from LLVM assembly and "
"provides details about the encoding of the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:36
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:39
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:41
msgid ""
"If {program}`llvm-bcanalyzer` succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if "
"an error occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value, usually 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:44
msgid "SUMMARY OUTPUT DEFINITIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:46
msgid ""
"The following items are always printed by llvm-bcanalyzer. They comprize the "
"summary output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:49
msgid "**Bitcode Analysis Of Module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:50
msgid ""
"This just provides the name of the module for which bitcode analysis is "
"being generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:53
msgid "**Bitcode Version Number**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:54
msgid ""
"The bitcode version (not LLVM version) of the file read by the analyzer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:56
msgid "**File Size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:57
msgid "The size, in bytes, of the entire bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:59
msgid "**Module Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:60
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of the module block. Percentage is relative to File Size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:62
msgid "**Function Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:63
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of all the function blocks. Percentage is relative to "
"File Size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:66
msgid "**Global Types Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:67
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of the Global Types Pool. Percentage is relative to File "
"Size. This is the size of the definitions of all types in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:70
msgid "**Constant Pool Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:71
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of the Constant Pool Blocks Percentage is relative to "
"File Size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:74
msgid "**Module Globals Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:75
msgid ""
"Ths size, in bytes, of the Global Variable Definitions and their "
"initializers. Percentage is relative to File Size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:78
msgid "**Instruction List Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:79
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of all the instruction lists in all the functions. "
"Percentage is relative to File Size. Note that this value is also included "
"in the Function Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:83
msgid "**Compaction Table Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:84
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of all the compaction tables in all the functions. "
"Percentage is relative to File Size. Note that this value is also included "
"in the Function Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:88
msgid "**Symbol Table Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:89
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of all the symbol tables in all the functions. "
"Percentage is relative to File Size. Note that this value is also included "
"in the Function Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:93
msgid "**Dependent Libraries Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:94
msgid ""
"The size, in bytes, of the list of dependent libraries in the module. "
"Percentage is relative to File Size. Note that this value is also included "
"in the Module Global Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:98
msgid "**Number Of Bitcode Blocks**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:99
msgid "The total number of blocks of any kind in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:101
msgid "**Number Of Functions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:102
msgid "The total number of function definitions in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:104
msgid "**Number Of Types**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:105
msgid "The total number of types defined in the Global Types Pool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:107
msgid "**Number Of Constants**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:108
msgid ""
"The total number of constants (of any type) defined in the Constant Pool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:110
msgid "**Number Of Basic Blocks**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:111
msgid ""
"The total number of basic blocks defined in all functions in the bitcode "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:113
msgid "**Number Of Instructions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:114
msgid ""
"The total number of instructions defined in all functions in the bitcode "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:116
msgid "**Number Of Long Instructions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:117
msgid ""
"The total number of long instructions defined in all functions in the "
"bitcode file. Long instructions are those taking greater than 4 bytes. "
"Typically long instructions are GetElementPtr with several indices, PHI "
"nodes, and calls to functions with large numbers of arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:122
msgid "**Number Of Operands**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:123
msgid ""
"The total number of operands used in all instructions in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:125
msgid "**Number Of Compaction Tables**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:126
msgid ""
"The total number of compaction tables in all functions in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:128
msgid "**Number Of Symbol Tables**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:129
msgid "The total number of symbol tables in all functions in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:131
msgid "**Number Of Dependent Libs**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:132
msgid "The total number of dependent libraries found in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:134
msgid "**Total Instruction Size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:135
msgid ""
"The total size of the instructions in all functions in the bitcode file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:137
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:208
msgid "**Average Instruction Size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:138
msgid ""
"The average number of bytes per instruction across all functions in the "
"bitcode file. This value is computed by dividing Total Instruction Size by "
"Number Of Instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:142
msgid "**Maximum Type Slot Number**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:143
msgid ""
"The maximum value used for a type's slot number. Larger slot number values "
"take more bytes to encode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:146
msgid "**Maximum Value Slot Number**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:147
msgid ""
"The maximum value used for a value's slot number. Larger slot number values "
"take more bytes to encode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:150
msgid "**Bytes Per Value**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:151
msgid ""
"The average size of a Value definition (of any type). This is computed by "
"dividing File Size by the total number of values of any type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:154
msgid "**Bytes Per Global**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:155
msgid ""
"The average size of a global definition (constants and global variables)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:157
msgid "**Bytes Per Function**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:158
msgid ""
"The average number of bytes per function definition. This is computed by "
"dividing Function Bytes by Number Of Functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:161
msgid "**# of VBR 32-bit Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:162
msgid ""
"The total number of 32-bit integers encoded using the Variable Bit Rate "
"encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:165
msgid "**# of VBR 64-bit Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:166
msgid ""
"The total number of 64-bit integers encoded using the Variable Bit Rate "
"encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:169
msgid "**# of VBR Compressed Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:170
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes consumed by the 32-bit and 64-bit integers that "
"use the Variable Bit Rate encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:173
msgid "**# of VBR Expanded Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:174
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes that would have been consumed by the 32-bit and 64-"
"bit integers had they not been compressed with the Variable Bit Rage "
"encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:178
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:233
msgid "**Bytes Saved With VBR**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:179
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes saved by using the Variable Bit Rate encoding "
"scheme. The percentage is relative to # of VBR Expanded Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:182
msgid "DETAILED OUTPUT DEFINITIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:184
msgid ""
"The following definitions occur only if the -nodetails option was not given. "
"The detailed output provides additional information on a per-function basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:187
msgid "**Type**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:188
msgid "The type signature of the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:190
msgid "**Byte Size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:191
msgid "The total number of bytes in the function's block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:193
msgid "**Basic Blocks**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:194
msgid "The number of basic blocks defined by the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:196
msgid "**Instructions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:197
msgid "The number of instructions defined by the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:199
msgid "**Long Instructions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:200
msgid ""
"The number of instructions using the long instruction format in the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:202
msgid "**Operands**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:203
msgid "The number of operands used by all instructions in the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:205
msgid "**Instruction Size**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:206
msgid "The number of bytes consumed by instructions in the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:209
msgid ""
"The average number of bytes consumed by the instructions in the function. "
"This value is computed by dividing Instruction Size by Instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:212
msgid "**Bytes Per Instruction**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:213
msgid ""
"The average number of bytes used by the function per instruction. This value "
"is computed by dividing Byte Size by Instructions. Note that this is not the "
"same as Average Instruction Size. It computes a number relative to the total "
"function size not just the size of the instruction list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:218
msgid "**Number of VBR 32-bit Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:219
msgid ""
"The total number of 32-bit integers found in this function (for any use)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:221
msgid "**Number of VBR 64-bit Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:222
msgid ""
"The total number of 64-bit integers found in this function (for any use)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:224
msgid "**Number of VBR Compressed Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:225
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes in this function consumed by the 32-bit and 64-bit "
"integers that use the Variable Bit Rate encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:228
msgid "**Number of VBR Expanded Bytes**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:229
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes in this function that would have been consumed by "
"the 32-bit and 64-bit integers had they not been compressed with the "
"Variable Bit Rate encoding scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:234
msgid ""
"The total number of bytes saved in this function by using the Variable Bit "
"Rate encoding scheme. The percentage is relative to # of VBR Expanded Bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-bcanalyzer.md:237
msgid "SEE ALSO"
msgstr ""

